  "source": "VEHICLES.md §3.2, §9.1. Modules a ship's sockets take: each an item, its frame's origin at its socket (a bay's rear centre on the deck, +Z forward, +Y up, +X the left side), its first part its body (a ball for the interact key and the hammer; its hull boxes for shots and blasts). The TOGG's (V2): a one-seat cab whose seat drives when it is the front-most cab on level 1, reached through its door, and an engine that goes in a bay or the nose mount; its running gear (VEHICLES.md §9.11) on the ground sockets: the stock tyres or the monster tyres, which need the lift kit (it raises the body 0.75 m and draws the Monster TOGG's frame). A module's ground, drag, crash and fuelUse blocks replace the kind's numbers while it is fitted (ShipTuning). Numbers are VEHICLES.md's starting values.",
